	<!-- ============================= ABOUT ============================= -->
	<item>
		<title>About</title>
		<link>https://j.langschwerts.de/about/</link>
		<pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[julian]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://j.langschwerts.de/?page_id=1002</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<!-- wp:paragraph {"fontSize":"large"} -->
<p class="has-large-font-size">I study data science at the University of Salzburg, with a focus on reinforcement learning, and work as a junior researcher in Information Technologies at FH Salzburg.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What draws me to reinforcement learning is not games but measurement. A model of a physical system is only as good as the data you gathered to fit it, and gathering that data is expensive &#8212; every experiment costs machine time. My master's thesis asks whether an agent can learn to choose those experiments well: not a fixed excitation signal decided in advance, but a policy that adapts as it learns what it still does not know about the system. That puts optimal experiment design and system identification in the same loop.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>I do this work alongside the IDA Lab and Simon Hirl&#228;nder, and within the ISIA project at FH Salzburg.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Outside research I build things that are useful to somebody specific: a tracker for a handball team, a game that makes art history stick. Both are listed under <a href="/projects/">Projects</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:separator -->
<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

