	<!-- ============================= HANDBALL TRACKER ============================= -->
	<item>
		<title>Handball Tracker</title>
		<link>https://j.langschwerts.de/projects/handball-tracker/</link>
		<pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[julian]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://j.langschwerts.de/?page_id=1006</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<!-- wp:paragraph {"fontSize":"large"} -->
<p class="has-large-font-size">A tracker for handball teams that lives on a Raspberry Pi and talks to players where they already are.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph {"style":{"typography":{"fontStyle":"italic","fontWeight":"400"}}} -->
<p style="font-style:italic;font-weight:400">In development &#8212; not yet publicly available.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The idea</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Amateur clubs run on group chats and somebody's memory. Attendance for training, who is injured, who is available on Saturday &#8212; it all lives in a scroll of messages nobody can search. The tracker gives a team a small web app for that, backed by a server that reaches players through the messaging app they already use, so there is nothing for anyone to install and no new account to forget.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Built with</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A Node.js and Express server with token-based authentication, running on a Raspberry Pi so a club can host it themselves for the price of the hardware. Messaging integration runs through a headless browser session on the same device.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
]]></content:encoded>
